# Bokeh Layout: Site Embed Vs Analysis Figures

## Two layers

1. **SPA + Django-side embed helpers** — Responsive sizing, zoom layout transforms, focus/keyboard behavior around the embed, and job-detail chrome live in **`hpcperfstats/site/lib/machine/bokeh_plot_layout.py`** and the **React** job detail components / CSS. Accessibility for controls **around** plots follows **`wcag-aa-mobile-web.mdc`**.
2. **Figure construction** — `sizing_mode`, dimensions, themes, glyphs, and data downsampling inside Bokeh **`figure()`** calls live under **`hpcperfstats/analysis/metrics/lib/plot/`**. Changing those affects **all** consumers of that plot builder (API, possible admin or batch renders) and is a **larger visual contract** change.

## SPA `BokehEmbed` (viewport + stagger)

- **Canonical component:** `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/components/BokehEmbed.jsx` — all pages must embed Bokeh `json_item` payloads through this component (not ad hoc `embed_item` calls elsewhere).
- **Defaults (production):** defer starting embed until the wrapper **intersects the viewport** (`IntersectionObserver`, configurable `rootMargin` / `threshold`); after Bokeh `Document.idle`, apply a short **settle delay** before the global embed lock releases, to reduce overlapping `ResizeObserver` work across multiple plots.
- **Defaults (Vitest):** viewport deferral is off unless `deferEmbedUntilVisible` is explicitly set (so unit tests do not need IO); settle delay is **0**. See `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/bokeh-embed-defaults.js`.
- **Opt-out:** pass `deferEmbedUntilVisible={false}` only for exceptional cases (e.g. hidden iframe / print).
- **Popover / dialog plots:** `HistogramThumbnails` gates the full-size embed until the popover plot container has layout (see same component). Do not mount `BokehEmbed` into a zero-size dialog subtree.
- **Global `ResizeObserver` patch:** `patch-resize-observer-for-bokeh.js` (applied from `main.jsx` / `bokehInit.js` before loading Bokeh) defers **all** browser resize callbacks used by Bokeh 3.9 with **three** `requestAnimationFrame` hops plus `setTimeout(0)`, so `after_resize` does not run while axis `ranges` are still undefined.
- **Shadow DOM (Bokeh 3.x):** every `DOMComponentView` attaches an **open** `shadowRoot`; `CanvasView` appends `canvas.bk-layer` into its own shadow root. Any code that reads plot **pixels** or canvas geometry (Job Detail print capture in `job-detail-print-snapshot.ts`) **must** traverse `shadowRoot` — plain `querySelectorAll("canvas")` finds nothing.

## Bokeh version bumps

- Follow **`bokeh-version-and-vendor-patch-upgrade.mdc`**: keep JS (`@bokeh/bokehjs`), Python (`bokeh==…`), and the Playwright CDN pin in sync; run Vitest + the Playwright Bokeh embed module after bumps.

## When changing job detail plots

- Prefer **`bokeh_plot_layout.py`** + frontend for **container and zoom UX** without altering core plot semantics.
- Coordinate **`hpcperfstats/analysis/metrics/lib/plot/`** changes with **`job-plot-artifacts-caching.mdc`** (fingerprints / schema version) and any **roofline / monitor type** rules if data shapes change.
- **Job-list `job_hist`:** keep equal `min_border_left`/`min_border_right` and equal x-range pad (explicit `Range1d`); do not pad via HistogramThumbnails HTML/CSS.
- **TypeDetail (`devplot`):** match Summary — `figure_embed_kw` + `gridplot(..., ncols=min(2, len(plots)), sizing_mode="stretch_width")`.
- **Multiprecision pies:** fixed Bokeh sizing; SPA `PlotPanel` must pass `maximizeInContainer={false}` so wedges are not width-stretched.

## Overlap

- **`no-scientific-notation-web.mdc`** for axes, hovers, and tables.
- **`job-plot-artifacts-caching.mdc`** when serialized `json_item` output changes.
- **`bokeh-version-and-vendor-patch-upgrade.mdc`** when changing Bokeh library versions.
